{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_2ac222e63d4c9e0067d1f608e9f67c736a0f396603d09abfac433349ba4802b6", "title": "San Juan de Sicilia", "text": "The San Juan de Sicilia was one of the 130 ships that formed the ill-fated Spanish Armada of 1588. The ship was originally known as the Brod Martolosi, before it was seized to form part of the navy. It was one of 10 ships forming the Levant squadron, one of 8 squadrons that formed the entire armada.", "score": 26.1995}, {"id": "hp_doc_753ff5fe5920d976f19f86803a1bd7e7819e5937a3d1f09984488a4e64c19ca4", "title": "Church of San Juan Bautista, Dalcahue", "text": "The Church of San Juan Bautista de San Juan de Coquihuil (Spanish: \"Iglesia de San Juan Bautista de San Juan de Coquihuil\" ) is a Roman Catholic church located in the Chilean hamlet of San Juan, commune of Dalcahue in Chiloé Island. Commonly referred to as «Church of San Juan» —Spanish: \"Iglesia de San Juan\" —, is within the Diocese of Ancud; its construction was finished around 1887.", "score": 18.252}, {"id": "hp_doc_d3c969975c208631306f478efd7b8788d739af2c667384aae8f0ad54c4bdd574", "title": "San Juan de Nicaragua Airport", "text": "San Juan de Nicaragua Airport (Spanish: \"Aeropuerto de San Juan de Nicaragua\") (ICAO: MNSN) is an airport located in San Juan de Nicaragua, Río San Juan, Nicaragua. The airport was built in 2012 at a cost of almost USD 17 million.", "score": 17.7463}], "remaining_searches": 2}
